  "summary": "San Diego's Public Safety Committee approved continued use of 54 surveillance technologies including ALPRs, with Mayor Todd Gloria publicly endorsing the technology as a proven crime-fighting tool. SDPD reported ALPRs have aided 600 investigations, 420+ arrests, and recovery of 440 stolen vehicles since 2024. The city council will revisit ALPR use on Dec. 9.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "ALPR technology is a \"proven tool that's solved homicides, recovered stolen vehicles and stopped kidnappings.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "since ALPR was launched in 2024, the technology has assisted the SDPD in 600 investigations, including the recovery of at least 20 firearms, $5.8 million in stolen property involving 440 stolen vehicles and resulted in more than 420 arrests",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "The operation and access to ALPR data shall be for official law enforcement purposes only",
